# cp.async with an ignore-src predicate (PTX ISA §9.7.9.26.3.1): each
# copy's global row counts the lanes whose ignore-src is false, under
# the copy's own guard, and its shared row the lanes that run it. The
# cache-hinted copy's ignore-src compares the CTA index with a
# parameter, so without the grid its row is a bound. The global load
# bytes per CTA count the reading lanes: 256 + 64 + 128 B, and at most
# 64 lanes of 16 B for the cache-hinted copy; the shared store counts
# every lane that runs a copy, 2752 B. Under the record, over the
# launch, the cache-hinted copy reads on 64 lanes of CTA 0 and 16 of
# CTA 1: 2176 B in all.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cp_async_ignore_src.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cp_async_ignore_src.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cp_async_ignore_src.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cp_async_ignore_src.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-NCU "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_cp_async_ignore_src( // block 64×1×1 | shared memory 4,096 B/CTA | per CTA: global load <= 1,472 B; shared store 2,752 B; param load 768 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	cp.async.cg.shared.global [ %r6 + 0 ], [ %rd3 + 0 ], 0x10, %p2; // shared store [16·%tid.x + buf] wavefronts/req ? (wavefronts not modelled) | global load [16·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 8–9 (ideal 8){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p3 cp.async.ca.shared.global [ %r8 + 1024 ], [ %rd5 + 1024 ], 0x4, %p2; // exec 48/CTA | shared store [4·%tid.x + buf + 1024] wavefronts/req ? (wavefronts not modelled) | global load [4·%tid.x + param_0 + 1024] sectors/req 2–3 (ideal 2){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	cp.async.ca.shared.global [ %r10 + 2048 ], [ %rd7 + 2048 ], 0x8, %p2; // shared store [8·%tid.x + buf + 2048] wavefronts/req ? (wavefronts not modelled) | global load [8·%tid.x + param_0 + 2048] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	cp.async.cg.shared.global.L2::cache_hint [ %r6 + 3072 ], [ %rd9 + 4096 ], 0x10, %p5, %rd10; // shared store [16·%tid.x + buf + 3072] wavefronts/req ? (wavefronts not modelled) | global load [16·%tid.x + 1024·%ctaid.x + param_0 + 4096] sectors/req <= 17 (ideal <= 16){{$}}
CHECK: <block 0>  cp.async.cg.shared.global                 shared store 16 B                                                      warp: ? (wavefronts not modelled)  [16 * %tid.x + buf]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.cg.shared.global                 global load 16 B on 16 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 16)                 warp: 8–9 sectors (ideal 8)        [16 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.ca.shared.global                 shared store 4 B on 48 threads in 2 warps (%tid.x < 48)                warp: ? (wavefronts not modelled)  [4 * %tid.x + buf + 1024]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.ca.shared.global                 global load 4 B on 16 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 48 and %tid.x < 16)  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)        [4 * %tid.x + param_0 + 1024]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.ca.shared.global                 shared store 8 B                                                       warp: ? (wavefronts not modelled)  [8 * %tid.x + buf + 2048]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.ca.shared.global                 global load 8 B on 16 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 16)                  warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)        [8 * %tid.x + param_0 + 2048]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.cg.shared.global.L2::cache_hint  shared store 16 B                                                      warp: ? (wavefronts not modelled)  [16 * %tid.x + buf + 3072]
CHECK-NEXT: <block 0>  cp.async.cg.shared.global.L2::cache_hint  global load 16 B (predicated)                                          warp: <= 17 sectors (ideal <= 16)  [16 * %tid.x + 1024 * %ctaid.x + param_0 + 4096]
ANN-NCU: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_cp_async_ignore_src( // grid 2×1×1 | block 64×1×1 | param_1 = 80 | shared memory 4,096 B/CTA | per launch: global load 2,176 B; shared store 5,504 B; param load 1,536 B{{$}}
